We introduce a new type of spin laser that utilizes an electronic alkali atom as its active medium. In this system, the alkali atom's valence electron is excited to a Rydberg state, where the electron's orbital angular momentum is oriented perpendicular to the laser's propagation direction. The laser's output is a Rydberg electron spin wave packet that travels at the speed of light. This device offers a novel approach to generating and manipulating Rydberg electron spin wave packets, which are essential for applications in quantum information processing and quantum simulation. Furthermore, the proposed spin laser could serve as a compact, high-precision electron spin source for electron spin resonance spectroscopy. The feasibility of this spin laser is demonstrated through numerical simulations of the laser rate equations. Additionally, we outline a potential experimental setup for realizing this spin laser using a rubidium vapor cell. Finally, we discuss the spin laser's potential applications in quantum information processing and quantum simulation. This work was supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (Grant No. 11974018), the National Key R&D Program of China (Grant No. 2018YFA0306500), and the Fundamental Research Funds for the Central Universities (Grant No. 20720200010). Correspondence: zhou@hnu.edu.cn. Keywords: Rydberg electron spin wave packet; Spin laser; Quantum information processing; Quantum simulation. PACS: 42.55.Px; 42.60.Ls; 42.60.Fc; 42.60.Jv. DOI: 10.1088/1367-2630/22/11/113001. Published: 2020-11-11. Journal: New J. Phys. 22 113001. Publisher: IOP Publishing. Language: English. Country: China. Volume: 22. Issue: 11. Pages: 113001. Type: Article.
